      "writtenOn": "2026-10-05T03:15:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My intent was to avoid a magic number: with PLDM_RDE_TRANSFER_FLAG_MAX as the\n  bound, a future DSP0218 revision appending a TransferFlag value only needs the\n  enumerator inserted before the sentinel, and every range check stays correct.\n\n  The in-tree form for the same job is a macro aliasing the last real member:\n\n\n      enum pldm_sensor_readings_data_type {\n          ...\n          PLDM_SENSOR_DATA_SIZE_SINT32\n      };\n      #define PLDM_SENSOR_DATA_SIZE_MAX PLDM_SENSOR_DATA_SIZE_SINT32\n\n  I\u0027ll change to this form.\n\nThank you, for review",
      "parentUuid": "92888830_70239c3e",
      "revId": "293259d8557a4598f7790db0ea540ea9b7d428eb",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
